Weather App
===========

This project documentation has been split into smaller files under `docs/` for
better maintainability.

Overview
========

Weather App is a Go project that provides both a terminal client and a small
web UI for checking current conditions and forecasts. It uses the free
Open-Meteo APIs, so there is no API key setup required.

The app fetches location data through Open-Meteo geocoding and then displays
current weather, a 5-day forecast, daylight details, alerts, and a simple
multi-model consensus view.

Highlights
==========

- CLI and web interfaces from the same codebase
- Current conditions including temperature, humidity, pressure, wind, and UV
- 5-day forecast with precipitation probability
- Sunrise and sunset details with a daylight arc
- Weather alerts such as heat, frost, storm, and high UV warnings
- Multi-model consensus using ECMWF, ICON, Meteo-France, and MET Norway
- Web server caching to reduce repeat upstream requests
- No API key required

Project Layout
==============

- `main.go`            Web server entry point
- `cmd/cli/main.go`    CLI entry point
- `weather/`           Core weather client, alerts, consensus, and formatting logic
- `templates/`         HTML templates for the web interface
- `docs/`              Expanded documentation
- `run.sh`             Helper script for common tasks
- `Makefile`           Build, run, and maintenance commands

Docs
====

- docs/README.md        Documentation index
- docs/overview.md      Project summary and feature overview
- docs/setup.md         Setup and build commands
- docs/cli.md           CLI usage
- docs/web.md           Web server usage
- docs/operations.md    API reference, env vars, proxy notes, and limitations

Quick Start
===========

- go mod tidy
- make build
- make run-cli ARGS="London"
- make run-web

Requirements
============

- Go 1.21 or higher
- Outbound internet access to:
  - `geocoding-api.open-meteo.com`
  - `api.open-meteo.com`
